      <activity id="6b2b4070-c302-5bab-82f6-1c04bc954670" activityNameId="fefd722f-3644-5d51-857f-74ec4b722a8c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Printed wiring board, surface mount, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Printed wiring board, surface mount, at plant
The functional unit represents 1 m2 of a 6-layer FR-4 PWB, surface finished (mixture of Pb-containing and Pb-free methods), with soldermask, for surface mount applications, without mounted components. It is designed to be used in ICT applications.; UUID: 936cf293-e879-357b-a1ac-9ba3c4d3f741
The module represents a 0:100 mixture of the datasets “printed wiring board, surface mount, Pb-containing surface, at plant” and “printed wiring board, surface mount, Pb-free surface, at plant”. It is assumed that after 2023 updates, no lead containing electronics are used in the market.
Location: This module is based on information from European producers that are seen as representative for the global situation.
Technology: See included processes for the various surface finishing techniques.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: $ 18.9315 Billion in 1998 (includes all rigid PWB)
Sampling: Mixture of surface finishing based on assumption
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_936cf293-e879-357b-a1ac-9ba3c4d3f741.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
